course: dictionary
lesson: 3869
title: Frank: honest, or a name?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word frank has three jobs. Frank is a boy's or man's name, often short for Francis or Franklin. As an adjective, frank means honest and open: a frank person says what they really think, even if it is not nice to hear. Frankly is an adverb you say before giving your true opinion, as in «Frankly, I think it needs more time.»
explain: Context tells you which meaning you need. «Frank and Mia walked to school together.» Here Frank is a person, because he is doing the walking. «Be frank with me: did you break the vase?» Here frank means honest, because someone is asking for the truth. Ask yourself: is this a person, or is it a way of being?
explain: Adults sometimes use the phrase «a frank exchange of views» in news reports and official letters. It does not mean a nice, honest chat. It means a serious argument, where people say strong things to each other. This is a polite way of describing a fight, so always check the words around it.
fact: Frank is a name for a boy or a man, often short for Francis or Franklin.
fact: Frank means honest and open, saying what you really think.
fact: Frankly means «to be honest», and you say it before giving your true opinion.
fact: «Frank's, open countenance» means his face looked honest and open.
fact: Anne Frank was a girl who wrote a diary while hiding from the Nazis in Amsterdam. Her diary tells one girl's story to millions of readers.
exercise: Mum asks, «Be frank: do you like my new hat?» What does frank mean here? | *Honest and open | A boy's name | Quiet and shy | Bouncy and happy
exercise: Jo says, «Frankly, I think your drawing needs more colour.» What is Jo doing? | Telling a joke about colours | Asking the time | Reading a story aloud | *Giving her true opinion, honestly
exercise: Which word in «Frank and Mia walked to school together» is a boy's name? | walked | school | *Frank | together
test: «The coach gave a frank talk about the team's mistakes.» What does frank mean here? | Funny and silly | *Honest and direct | Very quiet | Late
test: Dad says, «Frankly, the film was too long.» What does Frankly tell you? | I am happy about the film | The film was in another language | Let us leave the cinema now | *Dad is giving his honest opinion
exam: On the news, officials say, «There was a full and frank exchange of views.» What does it most likely mean? | *A serious argument | A calm and happy chat | A list of names | A lost bag at the station
